{"name":"Poncho","hex":"#b49073","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"poncho","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A simple garment, made from a rectangle of cloth, with a slit in the middle for the head.","A similar waterproof garment, today typically of rubber with a hood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poncho"}],"entries":[{"title":"Poncho","blocks":[{"text":"A poncho is a kind of plainly formed, loose outer garment originating in the Americas, traditionally and still usually made of fabric, and designed to keep the body warm. Ponchos have been used by the Native American peoples of the Andes, Greater Nicoya, Patagonia, and the Valley of Mexico since pre-Hispanic times, in places now under the territory of Argentina, Bolivia, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Costa Rica, Ecuador, Mexico, Nicaragua, Peru, Uruguay, and Venezuela, and have also become familiar in parts of the U.S. A rain poncho is made from a watertight material designed to keep the body dry from the rain."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Chile%2C_Araucanian_Indians_and_gauchos_-_Racinet_%2870086930%29.jpg/330px-Chile%2C_Araucanian_Indians_and_gauchos_-_Racinet_%2870086930%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poncho","wikidata":"Q468794"},{"title":"Poncho (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Poncho is an action game developed by Delve Interactive, released for Windows, OS X, and PlayStation 4 on November 3, 2015, and Wii U on August 18, 2016. A version for the PlayStation Vita was announced, but was cancelled."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/94/Poncho_video_game.png/330px-Poncho_video_game.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poncho_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q30599808"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Carnicero_de_Bogot%C3%A1.jpg/500px-Carnicero_de_Bogot%C3%A1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Carnicero_de_Bogot%C3%A1.jpg/1280px-Carnicero_de_Bogot%C3%A1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Carnicero_de_Bogot%C3%A1.jpg/500px-Carnicero_de_Bogot%C3%A1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" A market scene, Ruana in Bogotá, circa 1860","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarnicero_de_Bogot%C3%A1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Mamacona_%281387%29-1-.JPG/330px-Mamacona_%281387%29-1-.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Mamacona_%281387%29-1-.JPG/330px-Mamacona_%281387%29-1-.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Peruvian chalán dancing marinera on a Peruvian Paso horse","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMamacona_(1387)-1-.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Cacique_Lloncon_aprox._1890.jpg/500px-Cacique_Lloncon_aprox._1890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Cacique_Lloncon_aprox._1890.jpg/500px-Cacique_Lloncon_aprox._1890.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mapuche cacique Lloncon wearing a poncho in 1890","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACacique_Lloncon_aprox._1890.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/APEC2004_Chamanto.jpg/500px-APEC2004_Chamanto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/A